<title>TURKEY: Turk Koc Hldg Q1 net profits up 67 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Koc Hldg Q1 net profits up 67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   258.82 vs    258.28</p>
<p>    Net profit		  2,588.20 vs  1,549.68</p>
<p>    Net sales		     388.83 vs    171.83</p>
<p>    Operating loss		424.70 vs    165.71</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	3,239.28 vs  1,973.92</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   0    vs	0</p>
<p>    Total debts		 3,078.55 vs  2,072.58</p>
<p>    Equity		     25,478.30 vs 14,844.09</p>
<p>    Capital		    10,000.00 vs  6,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Koc Holding A.S. is the parent company of Turkey's leading industrial conglomerate. Its main income is dividend earnings from 86 subsidiaries and affiliates, reported under exceptional income.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
